# ShopMyUniform — MERN + AI Support Agent

## Technology Stack
- Frontend: React (Vite)
- Backend: Node.js + Express
- Database: MongoDB (Atlas)
- AI: OpenAI API (integration pending)

## Setup Instructions (backend)
cd backend
npm install
# create a .env file (see Environment Variables below)
npm run dev

## Environment Variables (backend/.env)
PORT=5000
MONGO_URI=your_mongodb_atlas_connection_string
JWT_SECRET=any_long_random_string
OPENAI_API_KEY=your_openai_key

## Database Structure
- School: name, city, grades[]
- User: name, email, password (hashed), role, studentName, grade, school (ref), phone, address
- Product: name, description, category, color, gender, school (ref), applicableGrades[], price, images[], sizes[{size, stock}], isActive
- Order: user (ref), items[{product (ref), name, size, quantity, price}], totalAmount, shippingAddress, status, statusHistory[{status, date, note}], estimatedDelivery, paymentMethod

## API Endpoints

| Method | Endpoint | Auth | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| POST | /api/auth/register | — | Register a new account |
| POST | /api/auth/login | — | Login, returns JWT |
| GET | /api/auth/profile | ✅ | Get logged-in user's profile |
| PUT | /api/auth/profile | ✅ | Update profile |
| GET | /api/schools | — | List all schools |
| GET | /api/schools/:id | — | Get one school |
| GET | /api/products | — | Search/filter products (query, school, grade, category, color, gender, minPrice, maxPrice) |
| GET | /api/products/:id | — | Product details |
| POST | /api/products | — | Create a product (used for seeding/demo) |
| POST | /api/orders | ✅ | Place an order from cart items |
| GET | /api/orders/my | ✅ | List logged-in user's orders |
| GET | /api/orders/:id | ✅ | Order details + tracking history |
| POST | /api/ai/chat | optional | AI chat — works for guests (product/delivery/return questions) and logged-in users (adds order questions) |

## AI Architecture & Integration Approach

**Pattern:** function calling (tool use), not RAG/vector search. The data (products, orders) is structured, so precise DB queries triggered by the LLM are more accurate than embedding-based semantic retrieval.

**Flow:**
1. User message + 6 tool definitions sent to the LLM (`search_products`, `get_size_availability`, `get_my_orders`, `get_order_by_id`, `get_delivery_info`, `get_return_policy`).
2. The model decides for itself whether it needs data and which tool(s) to call — nothing is scripted with if/else.
3. We execute the real query against MongoDB via `services/productService.js` / `services/orderService.js` — the same functions the REST API uses, so the AI never sees different data than the storefront.
4. The tool result is fed back to the model, which writes the final answer grounded in that real data. Loop supports up to 4 rounds for chained lookups.

**Guardrails:**
- Order-lookup tools are always scoped to the authenticated user's ID from the JWT (never from the model or the message) — the AI cannot be prompted into fetching another user's data.
- System prompt instructs the model to always attempt a tool call for order questions rather than guess whether someone is logged in.
- Never invents stock/price/order status; asks a clarifying question (e.g. which school) when ambiguous.

**Tested and confirmed working:** product search (school/grade/category/color filtering), size/stock availability, delivery policy, authenticated order status lookup, and return/exchange process.

